		<= Top_sites $mol_view
			sub /
				<= Top_sites_title $mol_view
					dom_name \h2
					sub /
						<= top_sites_title @ \Best for content sites
				<= Top_sites_note $mol_view
					sub /
						<= top_sites_note @ \Ranked by categories won in Weight and Built-in.
				<= Top_sites_list $mol_view
					sub <= top_sites_content /
		<= Rating $mol_view
			sub /
				<= Rating_title $mol_view
					dom_name \h2
					sub /
						<= rating_title @ \All frameworks
				<= Rating_note $mol_view
					sub /
						<= rating_note @ \Ranked by categories won against every other framework. A category counts only the metrics both sides publish, so a fuller table is no advantage in itself.
				<= Rating_head $mol_view
					sub /
						<= Rating_head_rank $mol_view
							sub /
								<= rating_head_rank @ \#
						<= Rating_head_mark $mol_view
						<= Rating_head_name $mol_view
							sub /
								<= rating_head_name @ \Framework
						<= Rating_head_score $mol_view
							sub /
								<= rating_head_score @ \Categories won
						<= Rating_head_since $mol_view
							sub /
								<= rating_head_since @ \Since
				<= Rating_list $mol_view
					sub <= rating_content /
				<= Pager $mol_view
					sub <= pager_content /
		<= Method $mol_view
			sub /
				<= Method_title $mol_view
					dom_name \h2
					sub /
						<= method_title_text @ \How this is measured
				<= Method_text $mol_view
					sub /
						<= method_body @ \Every number on a comparison page carries the source it came from and the date it was taken, and a metric nobody measured is absent rather than guessed. The live cases are one scenario written once per framework, with the same steps and the same timings, read inside the frame right after the run. The sources of all of it live in the repository, so you can read them, run them locally, or open an issue if something looks unfair.
				<= Method_link $mol_link
					uri \https://github.com/b-on-g/smalljs/tree/master/versus
					sub /
						<= method_link_label @ \Method and sources on GitHub
						<= Method_link_icon $mol_icon_open_in_new
	Popular_link* $mol_link
		arg <= pair_arg* *
		sub /
